From: nixos-m4pro
Subject: [PATCH] apple: boot NixOS from extlinux without the EFI attempts

The default environment defines aurora_boot, so board_late_init keeps it:
only the extlinux boot method, no BOOTAA64.EFI load and no EFI boot
manager, whose failures were printed on every boot once quiet boot was off.
---
--- a/board/apple/mac/mac.env	2026-11-14 14:38:29.242190715 +0530
+++ b/board/apple/mac/mac.env	2026-11-14 14:38:29.246936552 +0530
@@ -2,3 +2,11 @@
 stdout=vidconsole,serial
 stderr=vidconsole,serial
 boot_targets=nvme usb
+
+/*
+ * nixos-m4pro boots NixOS from the extlinux menu on the ESP and has no EFI
+ * loader there: go straight to extlinux instead of aurora's EFI attempts
+ * (BOOTAA64.EFI, then the EFI boot manager), which only print failures.
+ */
+bootmeths=extlinux
+aurora_boot=bootflow scan -b; echo Nothing could be booted. Use the serial console or reset.
